207
00:16:03.195 --> 00:16:06.979
The propeller receives the gearbox
efficiency times the shaft's share

208
00:16:07.019 --> 00:16:12.688
minus the low pressure compressor:
4 583 kilowatts; note that the

209
00:16:12.728 --> 00:16:17.291
gearbox efficiency multiplies both terms,
as the official solution stresses.

210
00:16:17.341 --> 00:16:24.054
At Mach 0.8 the model is past 0.7, so the
propeller efficiency is 0.9 times one

211
00:16:24.094 --> 00:16:32.006
minus 0.1 over 3, which is 0.87, and the
propeller thrust is 16.89 kilonewtons.

212
00:16:32.056 --> 00:16:37.208
The choked core jet adds
13.38, for a total of 30.27

213
00:16:37.248 --> 00:16:41.823
kilonewtons, with a T S F C of
25.54 milligrams per second

214
00:16:41.863 --> 00:16:47.116
per newton: 21 % better than the
turbofan, exactly the official answer.

215
00:16:48.766 --> 00:16:51.367
Now the propeller stream,
from momentum theory

216
00:16:51.407 --> 00:16:55.157
with the full disc area,
12.13 square metres, and

217
00:16:55.197 --> 00:16:59.797
the cruise density of 0.365
kilograms per cubic metre.

218
00:16:59.847 --> 00:17:03.947
The disc velocity is 243.9 metres per

219
00:17:03.987 --> 00:17:08.359
second, so the induction
factor is only 0.033.

220
00:17:08.409 --> 00:17:13.404
The ideal propulsive efficiency
is therefore 0.97, and the loss

221
00:17:13.444 --> 00:17:20.768
efficiency eta L is 0.87 times
1.033, which is 0.90, below one

222
00:17:20.808 --> 00:17:24.670
as it must be: the official note
says this factor collects the

223
00:17:24.710 --> 00:17:29.088
profile drag, swirl and tip losses
that momentum theory ignores.

224
00:17:29.138 --> 00:17:33.433
The propeller moves 1 081
kilograms per second, so the

225
00:17:33.473 --> 00:17:40.041
total flow is 1 105 and the bypass
ratio jumps from 6 to 44.5.

226
00:17:40.091 --> 00:17:47.714
The efficiencies are 23.6 % thermal,
92.2 % propulsive and 21.75 %

227
00:17:47.754 --> 00:17:53.468
overall, against 17.1 % for the turbofan:
this is the promise of the propfan.

228
00:17:55.118 --> 00:17:59.008
Exercise 1 B converts the take-off
engine into an open rotor, with

229
00:17:59.048 --> 00:18:03.502
the rotor behind the gas generator,
driven by the low pressure turbine.

230
00:18:03.552 --> 00:18:08.917
The same power bookkeeping gives
14 413 kilowatts for the rotor.

231
00:18:08.967 --> 00:18:13.344
At zero speed the efficiency model
cannot be used directly, so we try its

232
00:18:13.384 --> 00:18:19.093
static limit, ten eta max times the
power over the speed of sound, 381

233
00:18:19.133 --> 00:18:25.896
kilonewtons, and compare it with an ideal
disc of the same area, 183 kilonewtons.

234
00:18:25.946 --> 00:18:32.915
The implied figure of merit, 381 over
183 to the power three halves, is

235
00:18:32.955 --> 00:18:37.433
about 3, which is impossible, since no
propeller beats the ideal disc: the

236
00:18:37.473 --> 00:18:42.225
algebraic model hides a disc loading,
and here the disc is too small for it.

237
00:18:42.275 --> 00:18:46.938
So, as instructed, we use the
figure of merit 0.75: the rotor

238
00:18:46.978 --> 00:18:53.539
gives 151.1 kilonewtons, and
the matched core jet 20.4 more.

239
00:18:53.589 --> 00:18:57.666
The disc velocity is the square root
of the propeller thrust over two

240
00:18:57.706 --> 00:19:02.798
rho A, 71.5 metres per second, so
the propeller stream is rho A v p,

241
00:19:02.838 --> 00:19:09.422
1 056 kilograms per second; the
thermal efficiency is 17.8 %, while

242
00:19:09.462 --> 00:19:13.989
the propulsive and overall efficiencies
are zero at zero flight speed.

243
00:19:14.039 --> 00:19:20.791
The total is 171.5 kilonewtons with
a T S F C of 10.75 milligrams per

244
00:19:20.831 --> 00:19:26.422
second per newton, a total flow of
1 120 kilograms per second and a

245
00:19:26.462 --> 00:19:32.675
bypass ratio of 16.4, and here eta
L equals the figure of merit, 0.75.

246
00:19:34.325 --> 00:19:37.217
Let us put the four results side by side.

247
00:19:37.267 --> 00:19:40.273
With the same gas generator
and the same turbine inlet

248
00:19:40.313 --> 00:19:43.205
temperature, replacing the
ducted fan by an unducted

249
00:19:43.245 --> 00:19:46.306
propeller multiplies the
bypass ratio several times and

250
00:19:46.346 --> 00:19:52.223
cuts the fuel consumption by about 20
% at cruise and 35 % on the ground.

251
00:19:52.273 --> 00:19:58.288
The overall efficiency rises
from 17.1 to 21.75 % at cruise.

252
00:19:58.338 --> 00:20:02.141
The price is the tip Mach number
limit on flight speed, about

253
00:20:02.181 --> 00:20:06.738
Mach 0.8 even with swept blades,
plus noise, the gearbox and

254
00:20:06.778 --> 00:20:11.726
installation issues; that is the whole
story of propfans and open rotors.

255
00:20:13.376 --> 00:20:16.223
Here is the second page
of your cheat sheet.

256
00:20:16.273 --> 00:20:20.017
The mass flows: core, bypass
and fuel referred to the core,

257
00:20:20.057 --> 00:20:24.192
the fan on all the flow, and
who drives whom on each spool.

258
00:20:24.242 --> 00:20:29.608
The procedure in one line, which is
exactly the structure of exercise 1 A.

259
00:20:29.658 --> 00:20:32.032
Momentum theory and the
propeller efficiency

260
00:20:32.072 --> 00:20:35.000
model, with the gearbox
in the propeller power.

261
00:20:35.050 --> 00:20:38.536
And the static case: the figure
of merit formula, the check

262
00:20:38.576 --> 00:20:42.061
that it cannot exceed one, and
the reminder that propulsive

263
00:20:42.101 --> 00:20:46.395
and overall efficiencies are zero
when the aircraft is not moving.

264
00:20:46.445 --> 00:20:49.154
In part three we go inside
the compressor and the

265
00:20:49.194 --> 00:20:53.134
